# Example environment for image-to-pptx (web app + CLI).
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. This file is committed, so it must never contain a real
# credential: a test (backend/tests/test_config.py) scans the whole repository -
# python AND frontend sources - and fails if a real key literal turns up.
#
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#   Copy it to .env (git-ignored) and put your real values in, then start the
#   stack. .env is loaded automatically - by ./run.sh, by `uvicorn app.main:app`
#   and by backend/cli.py:
#
#     cp .env.example .env     # then edit .env
#     ./run.sh
#
# PRECEDENCE: the real environment always wins, so you can override any single
# value for one run without editing the file:
#
#     GEMINI_API_KEY='other-key' ./run.sh
#     export PROVIDER_MODEL='gemini-3.7-flash'   # then ./run.sh
#
# The test suite deliberately does NOT read .env - backend/app/config.py only
# reads os.environ, so your local file can never change a test result.
#
# WHO NEEDS THE KEY
#   Required to convert an image: POST /api/convert, and the CLI's -i/--input
#   (backend/cli.py). Without it the API answers 503 missing_api_key and the
#   CLI stops with a message naming the variable.
#   Needed by NOTHING else: POST /api/preview, POST /api/build-from-json,
#   --from-json, GET /api/health and the test suite all work with the variable
#   completely unset - they build from a spec instead of calling the model.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# ONE provider is enough - Gemini is the default below. To switch, comment out
# every line of option A and uncomment one other option instead. Details:
# docs/providers.md. Works for ./run.sh, backend/cli.py and Docker.
#
# Without a PROVIDER line the first key present wins: LITELLM_API_KEY, then
# GEMINI_API_KEY, OPENAI_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

# Option A - Gemini directly (THE DEFAULT; free key at
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey). No proxy needed.
PROVIDER=gemini
GEMINI_API_KEY=replace-with-your-gemini-key
PROVIDER_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# Option B - OpenAI directly. No proxy needed.
# PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-with-your-openai-key
# PROVIDER_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Option C - Claude (Anthropic) directly, through the official anthropic SDK.
# No proxy needed.
# PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=replace-with-your-anthropic-key
# PROVIDER_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# Option D - a LiteLLM proxy (OpenAI-compatible). These three lines are read
# only in this mode. The key is whatever the proxy expects (its --master_key /
# general_settings); VISION_MODEL must be a name the proxy serves - list them
# with: curl "${LITELLM_BASE_URL%/}/v1/models"
# PROVIDER=litellm
# LITELLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:4000/
# LITELLM_API_KEY=sk-replace-with-your-own-key
# VISION_MODEL=gemini-flash
